BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Mid-Autumn Festival
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTSTAMP:20260926T144323Z
UID:fecfc1d36a01906858beccb214bb@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Mid-Autumn Festival When: Saturday\, September 26th from 3:30 
 to 5:30 PM Where: Marble House\, 596 Bellevue Avenue\, Newport Tickets: $1
 5 Adults and Children (2-17) Free for Children younger than 2 Free PSNC Fa
 mily-Level Members Celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival on the back lawn of M
 arble House\, near the Chinese Teahouse. The Mid-Autumn Festival\, Zhongqi
 u Jie (中 秋 节)\, also known as the Moon Festival or Mooncake Festival
 \, is a 3\,000-year-old tradition from China that celebrates togetherness.
  For the fourth year in a row\, we invite you to a family-friendly celebra
 tion of this festival on the grounds of Marble House. Activities will incl
 ude participating in various craft stations that will offer lantern decora
 ting\, paper folding\, book readings and more. You can also enjoy eating m
 ooncakes\, traditional treats and tea tasting. The Rhode Island Kung Fu &a
 mp\; Lion Dance Club will perform at 3:45pm to open the experience and onc
 e more at 4:15pm. Lion dance is a festive\, cultural performance that comb
 ines the movement and spirit of kung fu with drumming. It represents posit
 ivity\, good luck and the warding away of negative energy. Preservation So
 ciety Family-Level members receive complimentary admission\, but advance r
 egistration is required. If you would like to purchase a family membership
 \, please click here.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/an
 nual-mid-autumn-festival/111759/
LOCATION:Marble House\, 596 Bellevue Avenue\, Newport\, RI 02840 Time: 3:3
 0 PM to 5:30 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/annual-mid-autumn-festival/1117
 59/
END:VEVENT
